# Files/dirs excluded from the published tarball (npm pack)
# This file supplements package.json's `files` allow-list.
# Anything not in `files` that npm tries to include via the
# implicit `**/*` default is filtered out here.
#
# ── IMPORTANT: this file ALONE IS NOT ENOUGH ─────────────────────────
# When `files` in package.json NAMES a path, npm's allow-list wins and
# `.npmignore` is ignored for that path. That was measured, not
# assumed: with only the `.npmignore` entry for `android/src/main/
# jniLibs/`, the pack still held all 43 `.so` files, because `files`
# names `android/`. B-027's fix was the matching NEGATION in `files`
# (`"!android/src/main/jniLibs/"`).
#
# So every rule below has a twin in package.json's `files` array, and
# the `files` entry is the one that actually does the work. They are
# kept in sync deliberately: this file documents the intent, and the
# `files` entry enforces it.

# The example app. It is a development harness for THIS repo — it is
# welcome in GitHub and useless (and large) inside a consumer's
# node_modules.
example/

# Version control metadata and local docs. Neither belongs in a
# published package.
.git/
md/

# Native binaries fetched by the postinstall hook at consumer install time
# (would bloat the tarball by ~68MB — the .so files are downloaded, not shipped)
android/src/main/jniLibs/

# Gradle build outputs (would bloat the tarball by ~400MB)
android/.cxx/
android/.gradle/
android/build/
build/
.cxx/
.gradle/

# Test + verification files (kept in source for typecheck, not shipped)
src/README.example.tsx
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
__tests__/
__mocks__/
coverage/
android/src/test/

# One-shot development patches that rewrite the library's own Kotlin
# source. They were used once during the V16.0.6 release and have no
# meaning to a consumer — a Python script inside an npm package is
# noise.
scripts/override_react_methods.js
scripts/override_react_methods.py

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*.log
*.iml
.idea/

# Kotlin compiler + lint caches
.kotlin/
captures/
local.properties

# npm metadata that shouldn't ship
.npmignore
.eslintrc*
.prettierrc*
.editorconfig
